{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 18, :comments ["Begot you — like ״ויקטן ילד את אלמודד״; it means: fathered." "תשי — you forgot. From the root נשה, like ״אל תט אל דרכיה״ from the root נטה. And the yod in תשי is like the yod in ״יו״ד מלפניך אל תמחי״, which is like ״אל תמחה״: the yod at the end of תשי corresponds to the yod in ״אל תמחי״, just as ״אל תמחה״ is the form without it."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :rashbam, :lang :en, :chapter 32, :notes {1 "The comment draws an analogy: just as תמחי (with final yod) is the same verb as תמחה (without it), so תשי (with final yod) relates to a form without it; the yod is a pronominal suffix, not a root letter. The elliptical comparison is rendered hyper-literally to preserve Rashbam's terse syntax."}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:39:50.120402341Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}